(5938650, 861975, 45764, '<td valign="top">Great job teamy... keep this up!  Very creative.</td>', 'Great job teamy... keep this up!  Very creative.', '2010-04-09 13:25:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5941724, 862334, 50526, '<td valign="top">2''s  and 4''s ?  Shame on you guys.. <br/>Awesooome shot!</td>', '2''s  and 4''s ?  Shame on you guys.. Awesooome shot!', '2010-04-12 10:00:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(5941827, 862640, 103142, '<td valign="top">The problem is, even when you''re going for DPC friendly, you''re still incredibly artistic. I would have zoomed in much closer, gotten the people just on the right, and spot metered it so they weren''t so backlit.<br/> <br/>But I like yours better! I love the silhouette, I love the "feel" of the moment. The reason it didn''t score well, imo, is because people were looking for a more difficult capture. It''s not hard to stop the motion of a person bending over. The only stop motion that probably counted was the dog on the right, and 1 out of 4 probably wasn''t good enough for most people. The shot is incredible.</td>', 'The problem is, even when you''re going for DPC friendly, you''re still incredibly artistic. I would have zoomed in much closer, gotten the people just on the right, and spot metered it so they weren''t so backlit. But I like yours better! I love the silhouette, I love the "feel" of the moment. The reason it didn''t score well, imo, is because people were looking for a more difficult capture. It''s not hard to stop the motion of a person bending over. The only stop motion that probably counted was the dog on the right, and 1 out of 4 probably wasn''t good enough for most people. The shot is incredible.', '2010-04-12 11:04:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(5941870, 862640, 15711, '<td valign="top">Great moment, Deb.  I kinda see why it didn''t epitomize stop action but it really does when you think about it again.  I think people want a faster action to be stopped.  HEE HEE  I''m such a fan of silhouettes.</td>', 'Great moment, Deb.  I kinda see why it didn''t epitomize stop action but it really does when you think about it again.  I think people want a faster action to be stopped.  HEE HEE  I''m such a fan of silhouettes.', '2010-04-12 11:20:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(5946457, 862571, 15407, '<td valign="top">...or parts a-flyin''&amp; burning!</td>', '...or parts a-flyin''& burning!', '2010-04-14 14:26:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5952785, 862287, 24642, '<td valign="top">Fín mynd, stemming og litir.</td>', 'Fín mynd, stemming og litir.', '2010-04-18 21:12:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(5988040, 861792, 113479, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Abra:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by _smitty_:</b></div><hr/><i> thanks guys! yea im still working with the stock lens hopefully picking up a new one soon. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I know how you feel! 5 years of using the cheap Canon EF-S 18-55mm f/3.5-5.6 has not helped my wildife and macro yearnings but we must not blame our tools and do the best with what we''ve got.  Scew that! I''m going to sell the motor bike for some decent glass ;) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>haha yea man i hear ya on selling things to bvuy a new setup. im in the process of selling some things as well haha</td>', 'Originally posted by Abra: Originally posted by _smitty_: thanks guys! yea im still working with the stock lens hopefully picking up a new one soon.   I know how you feel! 5 years of using the cheap Canon EF-S 18-55mm f/3.5-5.6 has not helped my wildife and macro yearnings but we must not blame our tools and do the best with what we''ve got.  Scew that! I''m going to sell the motor bike for some decent glass ;)   haha yea man i hear ya on selling things to bvuy a new setup. im in the process of selling some things as well haha', '2010-05-03 16:10:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(6007356, 862334, 52995, '<td valign="top">Very nice work. I think I read about doing this in Practical Photography (or maybe it was a different photo mag).</td>', 'Very nice work. I think I read about doing this in Practical Photography (or maybe it was a different photo mag).', '2010-05-14 15:12:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(6013010, 861823, 108580, '<td valign="top">Only followed this up now Chris, damn fine shot mate. That D3 is worth every cent if it does this day after day for you. My vote was one of the 22...seeing as I hang out in seedy waterholes shooting gigs now and again and know what it''s like. My D90 does really great on NR but this is fabulous. No noise to be seen on this image.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-05-21 03:27:36.</i></td>', 'Only followed this up now Chris, damn fine shot mate. That D3 is worth every cent if it does this day after day for you. My vote was one of the 22...seeing as I hang out in seedy waterholes shooting gigs now and again and know what it''s like. My D90 does really great on NR but this is fabulous. No noise to be seen on this image.', '2010-05-18 15:19:45.000000', '2010-05-21 04:27:36.000000', 0),
